{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"placeSubviews","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"bounds","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Rect","text":"Rect","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4RectV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"proposal","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize","text":"ProposedViewSize","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI16ProposedViewSizeV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"subviews","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/Subviews","text":"Subviews","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI6LayoutP8Subviewsa"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cache","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/Cache","text":"Cache","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI6LayoutP5CacheQa"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The region that the container view’s parent allocates to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"container view, specified in the parent’s coordinate space."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Place all the container’s subviews within the region."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The size of this region matches a size that your container"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"previously returned from a call to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/sizeThatFits(proposal:subviews:cache:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"bounds"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The size proposal from which the container generated the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size that the parent used to create the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bounds"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The parent might propose more than one size before calling the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"placement method, but it always uses one of the proposals and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corresponding returned size when placing the container."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"proposal"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A collection of proxies that represent the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"views that the container arranges. Use the proxies in the collection","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to get information about the subviews and to tell the subviews","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where to appear.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"subviews"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Optional storage for calculated data that you can share among"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the methods of your custom layout container. See"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeCache(subviews:)-23agy"},{"type":"text","text":" for details."}]}],"name":"cache"}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI calls your implementation of this method to tell your","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"custom layout container to place its subviews. From this method, call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview\/place(at:anchor:proposal:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" method on each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element in ","type":"text"},{"code":"subviews","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to tell the subviews where to appear in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"user interface.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, you can create a basic vertical stack that places views"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in a column, with views horizontally aligned on their leading edge:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["struct BasicVStack: Layout {","    func placeSubviews(","        in bounds: CGRect,","        proposal: ProposedViewSize,","        subviews: Subviews,","        cache: inout ()","    ) {","        var point = bounds.origin","        for subview in subviews {","            subview.place(at: point, anchor: .topLeading, proposal: .unspecified)","            point.y += subview.dimensions(in: .unspecified).height","        }","    }","","    \/\/ This layout also needs a sizeThatFits() implementation.","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The example creates a placement point that starts at the origin of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specified "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bounds"},{"type":"text","text":" input and uses that to place the first subview. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then moves the point in the y dimension by the subview’s height,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which it reads using the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview\/dimensions(in:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This prepares the point for the next iteration of the loop. All"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subview operations use an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ProposedViewSize\/unspecified","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" size"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"proposal to indicate that subviews should use and report their ideal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A more complex layout container might add space between subviews","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"according to their ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview\/spacing","type":"reference"},{"text":" preferences, or a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fixed space based on input configuration. For example, you can extend","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the basic vertical stack’s placement method to calculate the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preferred distances between adjacent subviews and store the results in","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an array:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["let spacing: [CGFloat] = subviews.indices.dropLast().map { index in","    subviews[index].spacing.distance(","        to: subviews[index + 1].spacing,","        along: .vertical)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The spacing’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ViewSpacing\/distance(to:along:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method considers the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"preferences of adjacent views on the edge where they meet. It returns"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the smallest distance that satisfies both views’ preferences for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"given edge. For example, if one view prefers at least "},{"code":"2","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" points on its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bottom edge, and the next view prefers at least "},{"code":"8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" points on its top"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge, the distance method returns "},{"code":"8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", because that’s the smallest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value that satisfies both preferences."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Update the placement calculations to use the spacing values:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["var point = bounds.origin","for (index, subview) in subviews.enumerated() {","    if index > 0 { point.y += spacing[index - 1] } \/\/ Add spacing.","    subview.place(at: point, anchor: .topLeading, proposal: .unspecified)","    point.y += subview.dimensions(in: .unspecified).height","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Be sure that you use computations during placement that are consistent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with those in your implementation of other protocol methods for a given"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set of inputs. For example, if you add spacing during placement,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"make sure your implementation of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/sizeThatFits(proposal:subviews:cache:)"},{"type":"text","text":" accounts for the extra space."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Similarly, if the sizing method returns different values for different"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size proposals, make sure the placement method responds to its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"proposal","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" input in the same way."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout\/placeSubviews(in:proposal:subviews:cache:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Assigns positions to each of the layout’s subviews."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout"]]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/layout\/placesubviews(in:proposal:subviews:cache:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI6LayoutP13placeSubviews2in8proposal8subviews5cacheyAA4RectV_AA16ProposedViewSizeVAA0dF0V5CacheQzztF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","required":true,"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"placeSubviews","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Rect","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4RectV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"proposal","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ProposedViewSize","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI16ProposedViewSizeV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"subviews","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Subviews","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifi